SUMMARY:🚀 Falcon 9 · SDA Tranche 1 Transport Layer A
LOCATION:Space Launch Complex 4E\, Vandenberg SFB\, CA\, USA
DESCRIPTION:Status: Go\nWindow: 2026-10-05 08:16 to 2026-10-05 08:28 UTC\nB
 ooster: B1103\, landing LZ-4\nOrbit: Polar Orbit\nMission type: Government
 /Top Secret\nWebcast: https://x.com/i/broadcasts/1oJMvNEQewoxQ\n\nTranche 
 1 Transport Layer A is one of six missions by the United States Space Forc
 e Space Development Agency (SDA) for the Proliferated Warfighter Space Arc
 hitecture (PWSA) Tranche 1 Transport Layer constellation\, which will prov
 ide assured\, resilient\, low-latency military data and connectivity world
 wide to the full range of warfighter platforms from Low Earth Orbit satell
 ites.\n\nThe constellation will be interconnected with Optical Inter-Satel
 lite Links (OISLs) which have significantly increased performance over exi
 sting radio frequency crosslinks. It is expected to operate over Ka band\,
  have stereo coverage and be dynamically networked for simpler hand-offs\,
  greater bandwidth and fault tolerance.\n\nThis launch carries 21 satellit
 es manufactured by Northrop Grumman.\n\nUnofficial\, not affiliated with S
 paceX. Data: The Space Devs. https://launchcal.github.io
URL:https://x.com/i/broadcasts/1oJMvNEQewoxQ
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c6e0ad16-8a78-46bc-a693-fbbf5ea4db6f@launchcal.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261001T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20280705
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20280706
SUMMARY:🚀 Falcon Heavy · Dragonfly (TBD)
LOCATION:Launch Complex 39A\, Kennedy Space Center\, FL\, USA
DESCRIPTION:Status: TBD\nBoosters: TBD\, landing TBD\; TBD\, landing TBD\; 
 TBD\, landing TBD\nOrbit: Heliocentric\nMission type: Planetary Science\n\
 nDragonfly is NASA's 4th New Frontiers program mission that will send a ro
 botic rotorcraft to fly within the atmosphere of Saturn's moon Titan to sa
 mple materials and determine surface composition in different geologic set
 tings\, advancing humanity's search for the building blocks of life.\n\nTh
 e craft is a large quadcopter with double rotors with mass of about 875 kg
 \, featuring rotors of 1.35 m in diameter. It can fly through several kilo
 meters within an hour and will perform 1 flight per Titan day (~16 Earth d
 ays). During the planned 3.3-year mission\, Dragonfly is expected to cover
  distance up to several hundred km.\n\nDragonfly will use a Multi-Mission 
 Radioisotope Thermoelectric Generator (MMRTG) to power its instruments.\n\
 nThe planned science instrument suite is:\n* DragonCam: Camera Suite\n* Dr
 ACO: Drill for Acquisition of Complex Organics\n* DraMS: Mass Spectrometer
 \n* DraGNS: Gamma-ray and Neutron Spectrometer\n* DraGMet: Geophysics and 
 Meteorology\n\nUnofficial\, not affiliated with SpaceX. Data: The Space De
 vs. https://launchcal.github.io
STATUS:TENTATIVE
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
